# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mark Neumann et al. (2024). Orb: A Fast, Scalable Neural Network Potential.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2410.22570  arXiv:2410.22570v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2410.22570v1 (sha256 c7685a950b193d18...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 203 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/neumann2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the Orb architecture (introduced here; ORB in the
# registry), the universal Orb models trained on MPtrj and Alexandria
# (and on MPtrj only), the D3-corrected Orb-D3, and the four molecule-
# specific Orb models fine-tuned on MD17-10k. Results: the Matbench
# Discovery energy MAE and R2 (Table 1) and the MD17 test force MAEs of the
# fine-tuned models (Table 2). Stability, h(r), the zero-shot MD17 study
# (Table 3), MOF-5 MD and Mg-MOF-74 adsorption are not accuracy metrics of
# the schema; baseline values quoted from other papers are not encoded.

