###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Pretraining on 8 NVIDIA A100 GPUs, fine-tuning on one A100 (App. 6.2);
# durations are not given. Speed is reported only relative to MACE (3-6
# times faster forward pass at large system sizes, Fig. 3) without per-atom
# figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Orb is non-conservative: forces come from a separate head, with net-force and net-torque removal (Sec. 2.2, App. 6.3). The backbone is a Graph Network Simulator with smoothed graph attention; GNS is not a registry method, so no derivation edge is recorded.
# - Training-set sizes of MPtrj, Alexandria and the pretraining set are not given. The neighbour radius is 'a max radius of 10' with 20 nearest neighbours; the unit is not stated.
# - Matbench Discovery MAE and R2 refer to the energy above the convex hull after relaxation with Orb (eV/atom, no unit individual); F1, DAF, precision, recall and accuracy are classification scores and are not encoded.
# - Which Orb variant was fine-tuned for the four MD17 molecules is not stated; the base model is recorded in the encoding input as 'Orb (variant not stated)'.
# - The registry model ORB-MPtrj (label from its first evaluating paper, loew2025) is the MPtrj-only Orb of Table 1; this paper does not state its parameter count.
# - Orb-D3 is used only for the Mg-MOF-74 heat of adsorption (-54.9 kJ/mol against -44 kJ/mol experiment), which is not an accuracy metric of the schema.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/neumann2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

